+/*
+ * QEMU Intel 82599 (X520) 10 Gigabit Ethernet controller with SR-IOV
+ *
+ * The physical function is the 82599ES SFP+ part (8086:10fb) as an
+ * X520-DA1 carries it: one port, an SFP+ cage holding a passive
+ * direct-attach copper cable, the cable's SFF-8472 identification
+ * read by the driver over the I2C lines it bit-bangs through I2CCTL.
+ * The virtual functions (8086:10ed) are its 63 SR-IOV functions.
+ *
+ * What is modelled is what a driver for the part, Linux's ixgbe and
+ * ixgbevf among them, depends on:
+ *
+ *	the EEPROM, read through EERD, with its checksum and the SFP+
+ *	init sequence list the driver programs into CORECTL; the
+ *	software/firmware semaphores (SWSM, GSSR); a self-clearing
+ *	CTRL.RST; MDIO with no PHY behind it; AUTOC with its
+ *	auto-negotiation state in ANLP1; LINKS at 10Gb/s
+ *
+ *	128 transmit and 128 receive queues with advanced (and legacy)
+ *	descriptors, checksum and TCP segmentation offload, VLAN
+ *	insertion and stripping, receive checksum validation
+ *
+ *	interrupts in legacy, MSI and MSI-X mode: EICR with its
+ *	auto-clear (EIAC) and auto-mask (EIAM), the extended registers
+ *	for vectors 16-63, IVAR mapping queues and other causes to
+ *	vectors
+ *
+ *	virtualisation: pools of 2, 4 or 8 queues (GCR_EXT), pool
+ *	selection by MAC (RAR, MPSAR), multicast table, VLAN pool
+ *	filters (VLVF), per-pool offload (VMOLR), the enables VFRE and
+ *	VFTE, MAC and VLAN anti-spoofing, default VLAN insertion
+ *	(VMVIR), and the internal switch that loops frames between
+ *	pools (PFDTXGSWC); the PF/VF mailboxes with their ownership
+ *	bits and interrupts; VF reset, VF function-level reset (VFLRE)
+ *	and the PF reset indications the VFs see (RSTI, RSTD)
+ *
+ * Statistics are kept for the counters drivers read on every pass;
+ * the others read as zero.  There is no flash, no flow director
+ * filtering (its commands complete and are not applied), no RSC, no
+ * DCB, no IPsec and no timestamping.
+ *
+ * Register layout and semantics are from the 82599 datasheet and
+ * the ixgbe/ixgbevf drivers' ixgbe_type.h, regs.h and mbx.h.
+ *
+ * This work is licensed under the terms of the GNU GPL, version 2 or
+ * later.  See the COPYING file in the top-level directory.
+ */
